1
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:10,219
So have you found a band yet for your wedding?

2
00:00:10,594 --> 00:00:12,596
No. 'Cause I'm in a band.

3
00:00:12,721 --> 00:00:14,014
We really rock.

4
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:15,283
Yeah. I mean, it's inevitable.

5
00:00:15,307 --> 00:00:19,061
I definitely overhear some wedding preparation, but I'm fine with it.

6
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:21,730
<i>She hears me arranging my social life.</i>

7
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:25,526
And we both have to hear Dwight order deer urine over the Internet.

8
00:00:25,692 --> 00:00:27,069
So it evens out.

9
00:00:27,903 --> 00:00:29,321
Oh, I got the Save-the-Date. Yeah?

10
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:31,281
Yeah. Pretty stationery. Oh, thanks.

11
00:00:31,365 --> 00:00:32,991
I didn't get mine yet.

12
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:37,162
Oh.

13
00:00:37,246 --> 00:00:39,957
There are a few people I decided not to invite,

14
00:00:40,666 --> 00:00:44,044
and that might make things kind of awkward,

15
00:00:44,670 --> 00:00:46,046
but it's my wedding.

16
00:00:46,755 --> 00:00:49,925
And I don't want anyone there who has called me a hussy.

17
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:26,795
Yes, thanks. Fantastic Sams, Adult Cut Plus.

18
00:01:26,878 --> 00:01:29,464
Comes with a shampoo and blow-dry.

19
00:01:30,257 --> 00:01:33,385
We're doing ID photos today. Gotta represent.

20
00:01:34,553 --> 00:01:36,680
On or off? Off.

21
00:01:36,847 --> 00:01:37,848
Okay.

22
00:01:37,931 --> 00:01:42,561
Oh, what is on your face? Is that a disguise?

23
00:01:43,395 --> 00:01:44,438
Excuse me.

24
00:01:45,897 --> 00:01:47,149
Clown paint.

25
00:01:47,774 --> 00:01:51,612
ID badges are long overdue. Security in this office park is a joke.

26
00:01:51,695 --> 00:01:55,073
Last year, I came to work with my spud gun in a duffel bag.

27
00:01:55,324 --> 00:01:57,200
I sat at my desk all day

28
00:01:57,367 --> 00:02:00,662
with a rifle that shoots potatoes at 60 pounds per square inch.

29
00:02:01,204 --> 00:02:03,707
Can you imagine if I was deranged?

30
00:02:04,499 --> 00:02:05,917
That's a nice tie.

31
00:02:08,211 --> 00:02:09,254
Thank you.

32
00:02:09,338 --> 00:02:12,424
That is... Who makes that? I don't know.

33
00:02:12,507 --> 00:02:14,968
Do you mind if I wear that for the photo?

34
00:02:15,469 --> 00:02:18,013
Let's... Let's keep our clothes.

35
00:02:19,097 --> 00:02:20,724
It's like child abuse!

36
00:02:21,892 --> 00:02:26,313
I say, if Jesus saw that, he'd freak out! He'd freak out, Toby!

37
00:02:26,396 --> 00:02:28,023
I mean, on so many levels!

38
00:02:28,106 --> 00:02:29,959
And I'm supposed to work there? I'm supposed to...

39
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:31,526
What's the dealio?

40
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:34,946
Just letting Oscar vent a little. We would use the break room,

41
00:02:35,030 --> 00:02:36,341
but the photographer's back there.

42
00:02:36,365 --> 00:02:38,158
What's the problem? Angela.

43
00:02:38,241 --> 00:02:41,995
There's just a little dispute over a poster in their workspace.

44
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,163
Since Christmas.

45
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:44,873
So, what, you're having a little spat?

46
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:46,875
I forget, are you guys dating? No.

47
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:49,878
Michael, can I talk to you for a second, please?

48
00:02:49,961 --> 00:02:50,962
Yes.

49
00:02:51,171 --> 00:02:54,216
Here's how I usually handle this. All I do is listen, you know?

50
00:02:54,299 --> 00:02:56,551
These things just have a way of working themselves out.

51
00:02:56,635 --> 00:02:59,596
It's like if you write someone a letter when you're really angry,

52
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:01,449
they say to keep it in a drawer for a couple of days

53
00:03:01,473 --> 00:03:03,475
and then you just never end up sending it.

54
00:03:03,558 --> 00:03:05,477
What do you know about conflict resolution?

55
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:08,355
Your answer to everything is to get divorced. So...

56
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:09,564
Okay. Okay, what?

57
00:03:09,648 --> 00:03:10,728
That was the right decision

58
00:03:10,774 --> 00:03:13,044
for me and my marriage. Yeah. Well, that's not gonna fly here,

59
00:03:13,068 --> 00:03:15,779
because in this office it is till death do us part.

60
00:03:15,862 --> 00:03:17,823
Assuming that we don't get downsized.

61
00:03:17,906 --> 00:03:22,494
Pam, would you get Angela and meet us in the conference room, please?

62
00:03:23,328 --> 00:03:25,872
A "Mediators Toolchest."

63
00:03:28,291 --> 00:03:31,628
Okay. Well, before we get started, you should know

64
00:03:31,712 --> 00:03:35,507
that there are five different styles of conflict.

65
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:39,553
My Shaolin temple style defeats your monkey style.

66
00:03:39,636 --> 00:03:42,764
Can we go? I have a lot of work to do. No. This is important.

67
00:03:42,848 --> 00:03:45,767
Okay. The first style is lose-lose. What's the next one?

68
00:03:45,851 --> 00:03:49,396
Just hold on, please. Okay.

69
00:03:49,688 --> 00:03:53,358
If we do lose-lose, neither of you gets what you want.

70
00:03:54,359 --> 00:03:55,777
Do you understand?

71
00:03:58,029 --> 00:04:00,282
You would both lose.

72
00:04:00,824 --> 00:04:05,662
Now, I need to ask you, do you want to pursue a lose-lose negotiation?

73
00:04:07,038 --> 00:04:10,333
Can we just skip to whatever number five is, win-win or whatever.

74
00:04:10,417 --> 00:04:12,461
Win-win is number four.

75
00:04:12,961 --> 00:04:15,630
And number five is win-win-win.

76
00:04:15,714 --> 00:04:19,676
The important difference here is with win-win-win, we all win.

77
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:24,681
Me, too. I win for having successfully mediated a conflict at work.

78
00:04:26,057 --> 00:04:28,935
Okay. So this is the disputed poster.

79
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:33,940
Now, one at a time, I want you to express your feelings,

80
00:04:34,065 --> 00:04:37,194
using "I" emotion language,

81
00:04:37,277 --> 00:04:40,405
and no judging or "you" statements.

82
00:04:40,572 --> 00:04:44,618
I got this poster for Christmas and I feel I want to see it every day.

83
00:04:44,868 --> 00:04:47,412
It makes me feel like the babies are the true artists,

84
00:04:47,496 --> 00:04:49,873
and God has a really cute sense of humor.

85
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:53,210
Come on. Seriously, that? I don't like looking at it.

86
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:56,213
It's creepy and in bad taste, and it's just offensive to me.

87
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:59,007
It makes me think of the horrible, frigid stage mothers

88
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:00,926
who forced the babies into it.

89
00:05:01,009 --> 00:05:05,472
It's kitsch. It's the opposite of art. It destroys art, it destroys souls.

90
00:05:05,555 --> 00:05:07,808
This is so much more offensive to me than hard-core porn.

91
00:05:07,891 --> 00:05:10,769
Okay, okay, okay. Stop. Stop. Stop.

92
00:05:10,852 --> 00:05:15,607
Let's see if we can't just brainstorm and find some creative alternatives

93
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:17,108
that are win-win. Win.

94
00:05:17,192 --> 00:05:18,276
Yes. Thank you, Pam.

95
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:22,239
How about Angela makes the poster into a t-shirt,

96
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:25,992
which Oscar wears. That way he can never see it

97
00:05:26,076 --> 00:05:29,704
and whenever she looks at Oscar, she can see it.

98
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:31,790
Win-win-win. No.

99
00:05:31,873 --> 00:05:32,874
That's... No.

100
00:05:32,958 --> 00:05:35,210
Okay. Well, brainstorm. Own the solution.

101
00:05:35,293 --> 00:05:36,711
How about I leave it up?

102
00:05:36,795 --> 00:05:38,338
How about she takes it down?

103
00:05:38,463 --> 00:05:42,425
How about Angela can keep it up on Tuesdays and Thursdays?

104
00:05:42,509 --> 00:05:45,887
Okay. That is called a compromise.

105
00:05:45,971 --> 00:05:49,307
And it is style three, and it is not ideal.

106
00:05:49,391 --> 00:05:52,978
To sum up, win-win: Make the poster into a t-shirt.

107
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:55,397
Win-lose: Take the poster down.

108
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:57,399
Compromise: Tuesdays and Thursdays.

109
00:05:57,482 --> 00:05:59,568
And the answer is

110
00:06:00,819 --> 00:06:03,780
make the poster into a t-shirt. Win-win.

111
00:06:03,864 --> 00:06:04,865
Win. Fine.

112
00:06:04,948 --> 00:06:06,908
But... It is done.

113
00:06:10,328 --> 00:06:12,289
No, you're all good. Great.

114
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:20,630
Hey, Angela. I didn't have your zip code.

115
00:06:20,964 --> 00:06:22,549
Oh. Thanks.

116
00:06:24,885 --> 00:06:28,847
It was hand-delivered. But I did get a Save-the-Date after all.

117
00:06:29,973 --> 00:06:31,516
It's not my taste.

118
00:06:32,017 --> 00:06:34,144
You solved it? Yes.

119
00:06:34,227 --> 00:06:37,397
Well, good. We can throw that one out.

120
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:40,567
Are those all the other complaints? Mmm-hmm.

121
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:42,485
I would like to see those, please.

122
00:06:42,569 --> 00:06:45,739
I can't do that. You can't do that, huh?

123
00:06:46,114 --> 00:06:47,115
Okay.

124
00:06:47,198 --> 00:06:50,994
Now you and I have a conflict. I order you to give me that file.

125
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:54,039
That... Okay.

126
00:06:57,125 --> 00:06:58,793
There. No more conflict.

127
00:06:59,753 --> 00:07:01,796
I had to use win-lose on that. It was not pretty.

128
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,757
All right. Is that it?

129
00:07:10,597 --> 00:07:11,932
It's all Dwight's.

130
00:07:12,015 --> 00:07:15,477
Every Friday at 4:00 I have a standing appointment with Dwight

131
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,812
for him to file a grievance against Jim.

132
00:07:17,896 --> 00:07:21,149
I tell him that I'm sending them to a special file in New York.

133
00:07:21,232 --> 00:07:23,860
That box is the special file in New York.

134
00:07:23,944 --> 00:07:26,488
Oh, God. All right.

135
00:07:27,155 --> 00:07:28,949
Why do I have to do everything?

136
00:07:29,032 --> 00:07:31,868
Are you sure? Oh, he's sure. Just shoot.

137
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:38,416
This is from Kevin.

138
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:41,962
He says Stanley uses his Miracle Whip without asking.

139
00:07:42,045 --> 00:07:45,840
Meredith complains that everyone talks too loud in the morning

140
00:07:45,924 --> 00:07:47,842
and the lights are too bright.

141
00:07:48,259 --> 00:07:49,386
Creed...

142
00:07:51,304 --> 00:07:54,432
Creed is sick of looking at the redhead all day,

143
00:07:54,516 --> 00:07:58,436
and wants a seat facing the receptionist. Nice.

144
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:02,941
You will notice that not one of these complaints is against me.

145
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:07,070
Actually, I have a separate folder for complaints against Michael.

146
00:08:07,237 --> 00:08:10,031
This is January

147
00:08:10,824 --> 00:08:12,867
through March of this year.

148
00:08:15,996 --> 00:08:19,416
How many of you have, at one time, gone to Toby

149
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:21,668
to complain about another employee?

150
00:08:23,461 --> 00:08:25,338
And did you get what you wanted?

151
00:08:25,422 --> 00:08:27,465
Or were you merely listened to,

152
00:08:27,882 --> 00:08:30,260
you forget about your problem and you move on?

153
00:08:30,343 --> 00:08:31,845
Merely listened to and forgotten.

154
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:33,471
That is outrageous.

155
00:08:33,888 --> 00:08:35,598
I love this place,

156
00:08:36,224 --> 00:08:40,979
and it pains me to see all of the negativity festering.

157
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:43,398
Okay.

158
00:08:43,565 --> 00:08:48,528
Today we are going to get everything out of these files and into the open

159
00:08:48,737 --> 00:08:50,113
where it can be resolved.

160
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:53,783
All right. How about the Phyllis-Angela dispute.

161
00:08:53,867 --> 00:08:56,411
- You already did me. - That's what she said.

162
00:08:56,703 --> 00:09:00,874
The thing is, Angela, you are in here an awful lot.

163
00:09:00,957 --> 00:09:04,127
You have complained about everybody in the office, except Dwight,

164
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:07,881
which is odd because everyone else has had run-ins with Dwight.

165
00:09:08,214 --> 00:09:10,383
Toby, by the way, what does "redacted" mean?

166
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:13,470
There is a file full of complaints in here marked "redacted"?

167
00:09:13,553 --> 00:09:16,514
Yeah. It just means whoever complained came to me later and withdrew it.

168
00:09:16,598 --> 00:09:19,309
So, I just took their name off. Okay.

169
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:21,978
There were a bunch of complaints about Dwight

170
00:09:22,062 --> 00:09:24,248
that were put in the redacted file about six months ago.

171
00:09:24,272 --> 00:09:28,735
Wait. If someone has a problem with me, why would they withdraw it six months ago?

172
00:09:32,864 --> 00:09:34,157
Let's move on.

173
00:09:34,699 --> 00:09:37,410
I volunteer. Did anyone have a problem with me?

174
00:09:37,494 --> 00:09:40,038
All right. Pamela! Come on down!

175
00:09:40,371 --> 00:09:41,623
Let's do it.

176
00:09:41,998 --> 00:09:45,668
And... Okay. Just one complaint.

177
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:49,547
Actually, it has been withdrawn. So that is no help to us. Next!

178
00:09:49,631 --> 00:09:50,924
Wait. What did it say?

179
00:09:51,007 --> 00:09:53,885
"Does she have to plan her wedding on office time?"

180
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:56,054
"Shouldn't she do that at home?"

181
00:09:57,055 --> 00:09:58,098
Who else?

182
00:09:58,765 --> 00:10:02,060
Why don't we just warm up first? Warm up emotionally. All right?

183
00:10:02,185 --> 00:10:04,312
<i>I have this kind of big secret about Angela.</i>

184
00:10:04,395 --> 00:10:08,066
And I've been really nice to her, and I haven't told anyone, and...

185
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:09,984
What the hell!

186
00:10:10,235 --> 00:10:12,737
Here is a Kelly complaint.

187
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:16,032
"Ryan never returns my calls." Join the club.

188
00:10:17,283 --> 00:10:19,786
My voicemail's real spotty sometimes.

189
00:10:19,869 --> 00:10:21,913
I didn't file a complaint. I was just talking.

190
00:10:21,996 --> 00:10:23,414
To your HR representative.

191
00:10:23,498 --> 00:10:26,167
To my friend, I thought. I want that withdrawn.

192
00:10:26,459 --> 00:10:29,879
Fine. I'll take your name off so no one will know.

193
00:10:31,714 --> 00:10:33,550
Making progress. Yes?

194
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:34,944
- Dwight tried to kiss me. - What?

195
00:10:34,968 --> 00:10:37,488
And I didn't tell anyone 'cause I'm not really sure how I feel about it.

196
00:10:37,512 --> 00:10:40,014
That is not true. Redact it. Redact it.

197
00:10:40,098 --> 00:10:41,617
Well, I'm not actually making a formal complaint.

198
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:43,361
I just really think we should talk about it.

199
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:46,187
Okay. Question. When a name is withdrawn, does that also apply

200
00:10:46,271 --> 00:10:48,982
to the permanent misbehavior file in New York?

201
00:10:49,858 --> 00:10:50,900
Sure.

202
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:54,487
Stanley, you got a lot of anger under there, buddy...

203
00:10:54,571 --> 00:10:57,157
Hey, thanks for ratting me out. I didn't do it.

204
00:10:57,240 --> 00:11:00,511
I find that hard to believe, considering you have problems with every single person

205
00:11:00,535 --> 00:11:03,454
in this entire office except Bobblehead Joe.

206
00:11:05,415 --> 00:11:10,378
Someone complained that the men's room is whites only.

207
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:13,756
Stanley, you know that's not true. I didn't say that.

208
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:16,926
Then why is there a picture of a white man on the door.

209
00:11:20,847 --> 00:11:24,559
Okay. Phyllis, you complained that Angela is giving you dirty looks

210
00:11:24,642 --> 00:11:27,187
and you tried to get off the party-planning committee.

211
00:11:27,270 --> 00:11:30,440
I never said any such thing. Angela and I are close.

212
00:11:30,565 --> 00:11:34,611
And, also, Phyllis, Stanley says that you cry too much

213
00:11:34,694 --> 00:11:35,862
and that that bugs him.

214
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:38,948
Stanley and I are close, too. We sit close.

215
00:11:39,032 --> 00:11:40,074
Okay.

216
00:11:42,577 --> 00:11:43,870
Just take it.

217
00:11:45,747 --> 00:11:47,332
I can't believe Angela.

218
00:11:47,707 --> 00:11:50,793
And I went against my better judgment and I gave her a Save-the-Date.

219
00:11:50,877 --> 00:11:53,087
And now it turns out she complained about me to Toby.

220
00:11:53,171 --> 00:11:54,797
Well, it was redacted.

221
00:11:55,798 --> 00:11:59,093
Look, if she wants an invite, maybe she's just trying to be friends.

222
00:11:59,177 --> 00:12:00,845
Don't take her side.

223
00:12:03,306 --> 00:12:04,986
Well, what does Roy think about everything?

224
00:12:05,058 --> 00:12:07,538
I don't know. I try not to bother him about this kind of stuff.

225
00:12:07,602 --> 00:12:09,520
You mean, like your thoughts and feelings.

226
00:12:09,604 --> 00:12:10,605
Yeah. Yeah.

227
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:14,984
I know you keep saying it's your space even though there's no assigned parking,

228
00:12:15,068 --> 00:12:16,152
but I keep forgetting.

229
00:12:16,236 --> 00:12:18,488
Yes, that's the problem. I guess so.

230
00:12:19,781 --> 00:12:21,658
Okay. Well, all settled then.

231
00:12:23,868 --> 00:12:25,453
I don't like you.

232
00:12:26,412 --> 00:12:28,373
Okay. Ryan, you told Toby

233
00:12:28,456 --> 00:12:32,001
that Creed has a distinct old man smell?

234
00:12:34,337 --> 00:12:35,964
I know exactly what he's talking about.

235
00:12:36,047 --> 00:12:39,384
<i>I sprout mung beans on damp paper towel in my desk drawer.</i>

236
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:42,178
Very nutritious, but they smell like death.

237
00:12:42,762 --> 00:12:47,225
All right, Kevin. You are accused of making sexually suggestive remarks to Angela

238
00:12:47,308 --> 00:12:49,394
that made her feel uncomfortable.

239
00:12:49,477 --> 00:12:54,232
Solution: Angela, you are to make sexually suggestive remarks to Kevin

240
00:12:54,315 --> 00:12:57,860
that will make him uncomfortable. I accept your decision.

241
00:12:59,237 --> 00:13:02,282
Hey, you know what, Dwight? Maybe we should get our photo ID taken together.

242
00:13:02,365 --> 00:13:05,326
That doesn't make any sense. Well, it saves time, you know.

243
00:13:05,410 --> 00:13:08,454
'Cause we could just meet in the parking lot every morning, walk in together.

244
00:13:08,538 --> 00:13:09,580
Perfect.

245
00:13:09,664 --> 00:13:10,999
<i>Smile.</i> No.

246
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,459
I never smile, if I can help it.

247
00:13:13,543 --> 00:13:16,504
Showing one's teeth is a submission signal in primates.

248
00:13:16,587 --> 00:13:20,967
When someone smiles at me, all I see is a chimpanzee begging for its life.

249
00:13:23,469 --> 00:13:25,138
This came out really well.

250
00:13:25,847 --> 00:13:27,390
There you go.

251
00:13:32,103 --> 00:13:35,064
This is humongous. I am not a security threat.

252
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:39,235
And my middle name is Kurt, not fart.

253
00:13:39,444 --> 00:13:40,778
What did I write?

254
00:13:44,407 --> 00:13:46,868
I have another complaint for Jim's permanent file.

255
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:49,162
Talk to Michael. I gave him the box.

256
00:13:49,662 --> 00:13:51,122
What box?

257
00:13:53,624 --> 00:13:55,501
I didn't report your snoring...

258
00:13:58,338 --> 00:14:01,466
Over here. God, God, God!

259
00:14:01,591 --> 00:14:03,134
No! No!

260
00:14:03,843 --> 00:14:05,863
Four years of malfeasance unreported. This cannot stand.

261
00:14:05,887 --> 00:14:08,056
Okay. Calm down. No, you calm down.

262
00:14:08,139 --> 00:14:09,783
Whose side is Toby on? Whose side are you on?

263
00:14:09,807 --> 00:14:11,809
Hey! Him or me? Him or me?

264
00:14:11,893 --> 00:14:14,687
I cannot work with Jim anymore. Either he goes or I go.

265
00:14:14,771 --> 00:14:16,189
Dwight. Stop. You choose!

266
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:18,900
One of us is out of here by the end of today!

267
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:23,404
Okay.

268
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:27,867
I am not bluffing. Okay? Okay. Yes.

269
00:14:27,950 --> 00:14:29,230
Do the right thing here, Michael.

270
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:33,623
Okay. I have served you loyally for years. I deserve this. You know I do.

271
00:14:36,167 --> 00:14:38,920
You know, your ID says you're a security threat.

272
00:14:39,629 --> 00:14:41,089
You have till 5:00.

273
00:14:45,385 --> 00:14:47,095
Oh, look, Jim.

274
00:14:47,428 --> 00:14:50,556
There's a sales manager position open in Stamford.

275
00:14:51,224 --> 00:14:54,060
Want me to call Jan and tell her you're interested?

276
00:14:54,143 --> 00:14:57,897
I could put in a good word for you 'cause I'll still be working here.

277
00:14:58,398 --> 00:15:00,066
Transfer. Transfer.

278
00:15:00,149 --> 00:15:03,820
Everybody! Transfer! Transfer! Transfer!

279
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:07,031
Okay, you two. In the conference room with me.

280
00:15:07,532 --> 00:15:10,618
Nobody leaves until we work this out.

281
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:12,620
Cage match.

282
00:15:13,079 --> 00:15:15,998
Cage matches? Yeah, they work. How could they not work?

283
00:15:16,082 --> 00:15:19,293
If they didn't work, everybody would still be in the cage.

284
00:15:19,377 --> 00:15:21,129
Okay. So, Dwight, in your own words,

285
00:15:21,212 --> 00:15:25,591
"Someone replaced all my pens and pencils with crayons. I suspect Jim Halpert."

286
00:15:26,551 --> 00:15:31,013
"Everyone has called me Dwayne all day. I think Jim Halpert paid them to."

287
00:15:32,807 --> 00:15:36,394
Yes. 5 bucks each and it was totally worth it.

288
00:15:36,644 --> 00:15:39,856
"This morning I found a bloody glove in my desk drawer,"

289
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:43,192
"and Jim Halpert tried to convince me I committed murder."

290
00:15:43,484 --> 00:15:45,736
"I think he may be the real murderer."

291
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:48,948
"Jim Halpert said there was an abandoned infant in the women's room."

292
00:15:49,031 --> 00:15:52,285
"When I went to save the child, I saw Meredith on the can."

293
00:15:53,161 --> 00:15:54,287
Gag.

294
00:15:55,329 --> 00:15:59,167
"This morning, I knocked myself in the head with the phone."

295
00:16:01,586 --> 00:16:02,753
That actually took a while.

296
00:16:02,837 --> 00:16:05,756
I had to put more and more nickels into his handset,

297
00:16:06,215 --> 00:16:09,802
till he got used to the weight. And then I just took them all out.

298
00:16:10,178 --> 00:16:14,015
"Every time I typed my name, it said diapers."

299
00:16:16,017 --> 00:16:17,602
Just a simple macro.

300
00:16:18,561 --> 00:16:22,231
You know, these actually don't sound that funny, one after another.

301
00:16:22,648 --> 00:16:24,400
But he does deserve it, though.

302
00:16:24,484 --> 00:16:28,488
"By the end of the day, my desk was about two feet closer to the copier."

303
00:16:29,363 --> 00:16:32,950
Yeah. I just moved it an inch every time he went to the bathroom.

304
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:36,787
And that's how I spent my entire day, that day.

305
00:16:59,852 --> 00:17:04,106
<i>The Japanese have this thing called shiatsu massage,</i>

306
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:07,235
<i>where they dig into your body very hard.</i>

307
00:17:07,318 --> 00:17:11,072
And it is very painful and, apparently, some people throw up.

308
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:13,658
But the next day they feel great.

309
00:17:14,158 --> 00:17:16,786
<i>I've never had one. They sound awful.</i>

310
00:17:23,501 --> 00:17:25,419
Maybe Stamford would be cool.

311
00:17:27,505 --> 00:17:28,923
It's a good market.

312
00:17:30,550 --> 00:17:32,885
Higher volume. Yeah.

313
00:17:35,388 --> 00:17:37,306
Maybe we should both go.

314
00:17:37,515 --> 00:17:39,016
I have a girlfriend.

315
00:17:39,183 --> 00:17:40,935
Sure you do, Dwight. Sure.

316
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:44,647
Hey. There's, like, 300 more of these.

317
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:46,232
Let's get to them later.

318
00:17:46,315 --> 00:17:47,915
So, are you going to transfer Jim or not?

319
00:17:47,984 --> 00:17:51,404
Maybe. I haven't decided yet. Let's get to work.

320
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:53,698
I want an answer by tomorrow. Okay.

321
00:17:54,407 --> 00:17:57,785
Actually, tomorrow's not good. How about later in the week?

322
00:17:58,828 --> 00:18:01,539
Fine. Good. Okay.

323
00:18:06,419 --> 00:18:10,298
Hey! Wait. How about a group picture, while you're here?

324
00:18:10,381 --> 00:18:12,192
I can't. I only get reimbursed for the ID photos.

325
00:18:12,216 --> 00:18:14,719
Well, it's a computer camera, right?

326
00:18:15,303 --> 00:18:18,347
You mean digital? Yeah. It'll take like two seconds.

327
00:18:18,889 --> 00:18:20,016
20 bucks.

328
00:18:21,225 --> 00:18:22,268
All right.

329
00:18:22,351 --> 00:18:25,229
Everybody, come on! Group photo for the newsletter!

330
00:18:25,354 --> 00:18:26,939
You've gotta be kidding.

331
00:18:27,023 --> 00:18:28,566
Come on, everybody. Come on. Let's go.

332
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:31,444
Creed, Kevin, Oscar, <i>ándale!</i> Let's go.

333
00:18:32,236 --> 00:18:34,447
One, two, three, smile.

334
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:35,948
Try to smile.

335
00:18:36,032 --> 00:18:38,135
We resolved a lot today, everybody. Think happy thoughts.

336
00:18:38,159 --> 00:18:39,303
All right, I'm just gonna take it on three,

337
00:18:39,327 --> 00:18:40,369
whether you smile or not.

338
00:18:40,453 --> 00:18:41,746
One, two, three.

339
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:43,998
Good. Let's check that out.

340
00:18:45,499 --> 00:18:47,960
Okay. All right. One more. Take one more.

341
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:50,046
That'll be another $20. What?

342
00:18:50,254 --> 00:18:51,857
Angela, I want to talk to you about something.

343
00:18:51,881 --> 00:18:52,882
What? No, Pam.

344
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:54,008
I am.

345
00:18:54,091 --> 00:18:56,011
It's about the Save-the-Date. Pam, it wasn't her.

346
00:18:56,093 --> 00:18:57,178
What?

347
00:18:58,429 --> 00:19:00,681
I'm the one who complained about you.

348
00:19:03,267 --> 00:19:06,103
I didn't know that Toby was going to write it down.

349
00:19:06,187 --> 00:19:07,188
Good.

350
00:19:07,271 --> 00:19:08,631
I was just venting. Check that out.

351
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:10,249
You know, it was just... It was one day.

352
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:11,442
That's terrible.

353
00:19:11,525 --> 00:19:13,736
I took it right back. It was just like...

354
00:19:15,905 --> 00:19:17,114
Okay.

355
00:19:17,198 --> 00:19:18,282
Oh, dear.

356
00:19:21,369 --> 00:19:22,536
Okay.

357
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:25,081
We can do this. Come on, everybody.

358
00:19:27,625 --> 00:19:30,169
All right. Here we go.

359
00:19:30,753 --> 00:19:34,590
<i>It was really hard getting a good picture of 15 people.</i>

360
00:19:34,757 --> 00:19:38,010
<i>He would not give me a discount, and eight tries added up.</i>

361
00:19:38,094 --> 00:19:39,804
One, two...

362
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:42,431
Didn't say "three," did I?

363
00:19:42,515 --> 00:19:45,226
<i>But I'm sort of an expert at Photoshop,</i>

364
00:19:45,309 --> 00:19:47,353
<i>so it turned out fine in the end.</i>

365
00:19:47,436 --> 00:19:50,398
<i>When people work together, there is going to be conflict.</i>

366
00:19:50,481 --> 00:19:53,192
<i>You can't outrun your problems.</i>

367
00:19:53,526 --> 00:19:56,404
<i>Hey, Pam. It's Jim. I have a doctor's appointment in the city,</i>

368
00:19:56,487 --> 00:19:59,031
<i>so I probably won't be in till the late afternoon.</i>

369
00:19:59,115 --> 00:20:00,825
<i>Just thought I'd let you know. Okay, bye.</i>

370
00:20:02,118 --> 00:20:05,037
Okay, Jan will see you now. Oh, thanks.

371
00:20:05,246 --> 00:20:08,040
<i>And that is why the idea of a cage match</i>

372
00:20:08,124 --> 00:20:10,584
<i>is so universally appealing.</i>

373
00:20:10,751 --> 00:20:13,295
<i>But here's the thing about cage matches,</i>

374
00:20:13,379 --> 00:20:16,716
<i>sometimes you have to open the cage.</i>

375
00:20:17,341 --> 00:20:21,887
And that is something that Toby will never understand.

